    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.55, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"wrong_rating\", \"components\": [\"U4\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.10\", \"U4.11\", \"U4.12\"], \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"GND\"], \"observed\": \"On the DISPLAY sheet, BS0 (pin 10) is wired up to the VCC rail, BS1 (pin 11) is wired to a GND symbol, and BS2 (pin 12) is wired to the same BS1/GND node. The strapping therefore reads BS0=1, BS1=0, BS2=0, which is not the BS2:BS0 interface-select pattern the spec describes.\", \"expected\": \"The specification states the strapping is BS0 to GND, BS1 to VCC, BS2 to GND (BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0) to select I2C mode. BS1 should be tied to VCC and BS0 to GND.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`BS0` (pin 10) \u2192 GND; `BS1` (pin 11) \u2192 VCC; `BS2` (pin 12) \u2192 GND. That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration\"}, {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch sheet: BS0 pin 10 wire routed up to a VCC symbol at the top; BS1 pin 11 and BS2 pin 12 joined to a GND symbol near R4/R6 (BS0 10, BS1 11, BS2 12 labels on U4 ER-OLED0.96-1W)\"}], \"impact\": \"With the interface-select pins strapped incorrectly, the SSD1306 will not enter the I2C mode the firmware expects, so the OLED will not respond to the MCU on DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA and the display will stay blank.\", \"confidence\": 0.55}]}",
